## 5. AUTH & SECURITY STATUS

### What works ✅
- **JWT login** — real `bcrypt.compare()` against hashed passwords in DB
- **Token verification** — `protect` middleware decodes JWT, fetches user from DB with `-password`
- **Role-based access** — `authorize()` middleware checks `req.user.role` against allowed roles
- **Rate limiting** — login endpoint limited to 5 attempts per 15 min per IP
- **Password hashing** — `bcrypt.genSalt(10)` in User model `pre('save')` hook
- **Duplicate prevention** — unique index on `Submission` (student+assignment) and `Marks` (student+subject+assessment)

### Security Issues Found ⚠️

| Issue | Severity | Location | Details |
|-------|----------|----------|---------|
| **No registration endpoint** | Low | — | Only admins can create users. This is by design but means no self-service. |
| **No password change** | Medium | — | Users cannot change their own password. Only admin can delete and re-create. |
| **No token expiry refresh** | Low | authController.js:L5 | Token expires in 30d with no refresh mechanism |
| **No ownership check on faculty routes** | **High** | facultyController.js | Any faculty can delete ANY assignment/submission — not just their own. `deleteAssignment` at L123 does `Assignment.findById(req.params.id)` but never checks `assignment.createdBy === req.user._id`. Same for `deleteSubmission`. |
| **No ownership check on getAssignmentSubmissions** | Medium | facultyController.js:L56 | Any faculty can view submissions for any assignment, not just their own. |
| **Promote endpoint has no validation** | Medium | adminRoutes.js:L16 | `POST /promote` accepts `{ branch, currentSem }` with no Joi validation. Could be called with missing fields. |
| **Feed create has no validation** | Low | feedRoutes.js:L12 | `POST /create` and `POST /broadcast` accept body with no Joi schema. Empty title/content possible (Mongoose `required` will catch it, but error message is generic 500). |
| **Assignment create has no validation** | Medium | facultyRoutes.js:L29 | `POST /assignments` has no Joi schema. Missing required fields will cause a Mongoose error → generic 500 response. |
| **Student submit has no validation** | Medium | studentRoutes.js:L25 | `POST /submit` has no Joi validation on `assignmentId`. |
| **Hardcoded admin credentials in seed script** | Low | scripts/seedAdmin.js:L21 | `adminpassword123` is in plain text in source. Should be changed after seeding. |
| **JWT secret is weak** | Medium | .env:L3 | `rymec_2026_top_secret_key` is a guessable secret. |
| **.env is not gitignored** | **High** | — | No `.gitignore` file exists. Real Cloudinary keys + DB password could be committed. |

